content.thinking:
Need JS for ticker toggle, including swap icon pause/play. Also ticker padding-right so text doesn't run under button? The track is full width, button overlays right 44px; text passes under black button, okay visually. Could add mask fade? Not needed.

The ticker-toggle button is inside ticker but the track is first; absolute button. `ticker:focus-within` pauses when button focused—then clicking pause toggles class. But focus remains on button → paused regardless, so clicking play won't resume while focused! Because :focus-within pauses. Remove `:focus-within` pause or handle focus differently. Better keep hover and explicit toggle only; keyboard users can press button to pause, but while focused it would be paused anyway. If they press again to play while focused, focus-within keeps paused. So drop :focus-within. Use hover + is-paused. Also when toggled pause, set aria-pressed true, swap icon. Add JS.

Also note `.ticker:hover` pauses on desktop, so clicking pause may appear to do nothing while hovering; but aria state. Hmm hover pause is a common accessible-ish feature but persistent pause needs explicit. Keep.

Add JS:
```
var ticker=document.querySelector('.ticker');
var toggle=...
if(ticker&&toggle){
 toggle.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   var paused=ticker.classList.toggle('is-paused');
   toggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', paused?'true':'false');
   toggle.setAttribute('aria-label', paused?'继续滚动文字':'暂停滚动文字');
   toggle.innerHTML = paused ? play svg : pause svg;
 });
}
```
Replacing innerHTML okay, but simpler toggle two SVGs hidden via CSS. Insert both icons with classes and CSS show based on aria-pressed. Use CSS:
```
.ticker-toggle .i-play{display:none}
.ticker-toggle[aria-pressed="true"] .i-play{display:block}
.ticker-toggle[aria-pressed="true"] .i-pause{display:none}
```
Then just attributes. Add both SVGs.

Also reduced motion: ticker animation none, button still can toggle; okay but label says pause while nothing moves. Could hide button under reduced motion? Not necessary, but better hide via `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){.ticker-toggle{display:none}}` since no motion. Add.

Also if JS disabled, animation runs but no pause control. Fine.

